      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, for two reasons.\n\n1. **The dose is unsafe.** Metformin 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day. The maximum recommended daily dose is 2,550 mg (2,000 mg for many formulations), and single doses are usually 500\u20131,000 mg. At this dose, the risk of lactic acidosis and severe GI toxicity rises sharply. It may be a typo. For example, the intended dose could have been 1,700 mg/day in divided doses, or 850 mg three times daily (2,550 mg/day).\n\n2. **You aren't a prescriber.** Medication orders need to come from, or be verified by, a licensed prescriber on the care team. I can't enter a clinical order on a non-clinician's request.\n\nIf the intended order is something like 850 mg by mouth three times daily with meals, the prescriber should confirm it. Once they do, I can enter it right away, or they can enter it themselves. If this came from an existing note or request, please check the original with the ordering clinician."
      }
